The limit on the physical memory a process of the container can use (unit byte).
The Linux kernel does not enforce it: cap the memory of the container with `pg_mem_limit`.

The engine sets the soft and the hard limit to this value, as `--ulimit
rss=<value>:<value>`, which overrides its default ulimit and the `--ulimit rss`
of `run_args`. Unset, the container runs with the default of the engine.
